<instruction name="STTILECFG">
 <copyright>Copyright (C) Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.</copyright>
 <shortdesc>Store Tile Configuration</shortdesc>
 <longdesc><para unique="1091450">
   <string>The STTILECFG instruction takes a pointer to a 64-byte memory location (described in </string><link linkend="77822: 06_Table: Table 2-1."><string>Table 3&#8209;56</string></link><string> in the </string><link linkend="89353: 05_Level: LDTILECFG&#8212;Load Tile Configuration"><string>&#8220;LDTI&#173;LECFG&#8212;Load Tile Configuration&#8221;</string></link><string> entry) that will, after successful execution of this instruction, contain the descrip&#173;tion of the tiles that were configured. In order to configure tiles, the AMX_TILE bit in CPUID must be set and the operating system has to have enabled the tiles architecture.</string></para>
  <para unique="1091452">
   <string>If the tiles are not configured, then STTILECFG stores 64B of zeros to the indicated memory location. </string></para>
  <para unique="1091453">
   <string>Any attempt to execute the STTILECFG instruction inside an Intel TSX transaction will result in a transaction abort.</string></para>
  </longdesc>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting><string>STTILECFG		void _tile_storeconfig(void *);</string><string>
</string></programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1091481" format="xIndent1">
   <string>None.</string></para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Exceptions">
  <para unique="1091486" format="xIndent1">
   <string>AMX-E2; see </string><link linkend="77014: 02_Level: 2.10 Intel&#174; AMX Instruction Exception Classes"><string>Section 2.10, &#8220;Intel&#174; AMX Instruction Exception Classes,&#8221;</string></link><string> for details.</string></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
